    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas V2 uses token buckets shared by endpoint set and resource scope; one uniform project-wide request limit does not describe the API. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/api/api-rate-limit.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:496341ac4b39984fd6921e2d77e5cf70d21a473caf14f84c2159e3901755e1fe",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:d2200987d8e97b21e20a36a8e1a929c4cef5dfa1bd1b08f914f4e3df0cb509ee"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "RateLimit-Limit describes burst capacity, RateLimit-Remaining available tokens, and Retry-After a minimum delay in seconds after throttling; clients must tolerate absent headers. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/api/api-rate-limit.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9f60b0221767cb9469ee7194f21a38e6164199762845cb99fd9ee344ef2200dd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:342d5dfc9e4240228df89f9d3d6949737bb0cd10be754a3813d715ccc8bbfdd2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Microsoft’s Atlas discovery integration distinguishes temporary rate-limit failures from authentication and permission failures, and lets users retry one credential without rechecking every credential. (low confidence)",
